# scripts/opcount: `collectbench bench reslice N` builds a fresh line of 80
# elements per 64 elements, collects 64 of them and grows the result by
# one (GP-RESLICE); the cost of one element is the slope between the two
# sizes. The control copies the part into a slice made to size, as Go
# must when it cannot prove the line dead.
unit element
sizes 409600 2457600
args bench reslice {n}
control benchmarks/collect/testdata/control
